# Language features on net48 / netstandard2.0

Many projects here target `net48` or `netstandard2.0` (alone or next to `net9.0`; check `<TargetFramework(s)>` in the
`.csproj` before writing new types). Those frameworks lack `System.Runtime.CompilerServices.IsExternalInit`, so
`init` accessors and `record` types fail the net48 build with CS0518, though the net9.0 build passes.

- Use `{ get; set; }` (or a constructor) instead of `init`, and a class instead of `record`, in such projects.
- Only `Clients/Viking/NGVV`, `Clients/Viking/WebAnnotation` and `Servers/SectionCorrection` carry an
  `IsExternalInit.cs` polyfill; don't add another just to use `init`.
- Collection expressions (`[]`, `[.. x]`) and other syntax-only features build fine.
- Build every target before committing (`dotnet build <proj>` with no `-f`), not only net9.0.
